# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Calendra — environment variables
#
# EVERY variable here is optional. The app is designed so that each one degrades to
# something honest rather than to a crash (ARCHITECTURE.md §10):
#
#   no AUTH_SECRET     → sessions signed with a development key, reported as unconfigured
#   no Google pair     → Sign in with Google hides itself; demo sessions remain
#   no model key       → the deterministic local reasoner; scheduling is identical
#   no STRIPE keys     → pricing shows a waitlist instead of a checkout
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. In Vercel, add them under
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables, then redeploy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Sessions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs the session cookie (HMAC-SHA256). REQUIRED in production: without it,
# sessions are signed with a public development key, which anyone can forge.
# Generate:  openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET=

# Set to "true" to make /planner private: no session → redirect to /signin, decided
# on the server before any client bundle is sent. Leave unset for an open demo.
REQUIRE_AUTH=

# ── Google (identity + calendar) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# One OAuth client powers both grants, which are requested separately and at
# different moments: identity at sign-up, calendar only when the user clicks
# "Connect Google Calendar".
#
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials →
# OAuth client ID → Web application. Then add BOTH authorised redirect URIs:
#
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback        (sign-in)
#   http://localhost:3000/api/calendar/callback    (calendar grant)
#
# …and the production equivalents, e.g.
#   https://your-domain.com/api/auth/callback
#   https://your-domain.com/api/calendar/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional. Defaults to <your-origin>/api/auth/callback. Set it when the public
# origin differs from the one Next serves (proxy, preview deployment, custom domain).
AUTH_REDIRECT_URI=

# Optional. Defaults to <your-origin>/api/calendar/callback. Must match one of the
# redirect URIs registered on the OAuth client exactly, scheme and path included.
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=

# ── Language model (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Omit entirely to run the deterministic local reasoner — the planner is fully
# functional and the schedule is identical. A live key makes the agent better at
# unusual phrasing, and the app falls back to the local path and says so on failure.
#
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai          # openai | anthropic | google | local
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini        # any model id the provider accepts

# ── Billing (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app ships no payment integration. When these are present the pricing page
# renders checkout; when they are absent it renders a waitlist and says why, rather
# than offering a button that does nothing.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=
# STRIPE_PRICE_TEAM=

# ── Runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auto-enabled when no model key is present. Set to "false" to hide demo data and
# the demo banner on a deployment you have fully configured.
# DEMO_MODE=true
